Subject: Keep Error.stackTraceLimit frames when the first level is skipped

What this does
  Collects one frame more than the stack trace limit when the backtrace skips
  its first level, and every frame that fits when a filter function is given.

Why we need it
  The logical stack walk stops collecting at the limit, and the loop that
  prints the frames then drops the first one: the Error constructor's own frame
  for `new Error()`. So `Error.stackTraceLimit = N` gave N - 1 frames where node
  and the stock engine give N. A filter function deeper than the limit was not
  found at all, and the trace started from the innermost frame instead.

What it adds
  Nothing new. The collection bound changes, the frames printed do not.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

Notes
  The frame buffer grows by one so a limit at its maximum still has room for
  the skipped frame. tests/differential/corpus/throw.js covers it.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 5a94df1..3994a9b 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -11603,10 +11603,19 @@ static void build_backtrace(JSContext *ctx, JSValueConst error_val,
        A light frame's function is `f->func` and its pc comes from its captured
        `cap_ip`. */
     {
-        JSRegBtFrame bt[64];
-        int nb, bi;
-
-        nb = regvm_fill_backtrace_frames(rt, bt, (int)stack_trace_limit);
+        /* One more than csd, for the frame SKIP_FIRST_LEVEL drops. */
+        JSRegBtFrame bt[countof(csd) + 1];
+        int nb, bi, max_bt;
+
+        /* The limit counts the frames that are printed, so collect the frame
+           the loop skips on top of it. A filter function may sit anywhere in
+           the stack, so its search gets every frame that fits. */
+        max_bt = stack_trace_limit;
+        if (has_filter_func)
+            max_bt = countof(bt);
+        else if (backtrace_flags & JS_BACKTRACE_FLAG_SKIP_FIRST_LEVEL)
+            max_bt++;
+        nb = regvm_fill_backtrace_frames(rt, bt, min_int(max_bt, countof(bt)));
 
         /* Find the frame we want to start from. Note that when a filter is used
            the filter function will be the first, but we also specify we want to
